{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37145096",
      "title": "Explicit Animations: Playing the Animation with AnimatedBuilder",
      "lectureOrder": 202,
      "videoOrder": 186,
      "sourceHash": "950563289298a4702499f4f2ad29a1ae39d7eaab91c4666c89ec90ae45d6cf17",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "So how can we now use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "this animation controller?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "Well, I mentioned that behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "it would update the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "and kind of re-execute the build method therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 16.14,
          "en": "Now technically that's not entirely correct though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.14,
          "end": 18.09,
          "en": "because if it would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.09,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "it would mean that everything in the build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 25.64,
          "en": "is rebuilt and reevaluated 60 times per second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "If you have a frame rate of 60 frames,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 30.42,
          "en": "and whilst you want to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.42,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "for the things you're animating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "you might not want to do that for all the other things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 36.603,
          "en": "that might be on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "For this screen here, it actually doesn't matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 42.87,
          "en": "because here I do only return this grid view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.87,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "which I do want to animate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 46.32,
          "en": "There is nothing else here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.32,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "but for other screens it might matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "So therefore, animated controller does actually not call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "build multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 56.97,
          "en": "but instead you can think of it as a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.97,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "or an interval running behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 60.99,
          "en": "to which you can listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "to then manually update parts of the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "And you can listen and update parts of the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "by using another widget provided by Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 73.203,
          "en": "the Animated Builder widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.155,
          "end": 77.752,
          "en": "This Animated Builder widget wants an animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.752,
          "end": 79.674,
          "en": "and a builder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.674,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "Now the animation is a listenable object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "and as it turns out, our animation controller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 90.48,
          "en": "is such a listenable object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.48,
          "end": 93.75,
          "en": "So we can pass our animation controller as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.75,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "for animation to Animated Builder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 98.32,
          "en": "and behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.233,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "this will basically tell Animated Builder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "when it should call this builder function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.13,
          "en": "because this function which we pass to builder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.13,
          "end": 109.77000000000001,
          "en": "this function here, will then be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.77000000000001,
          "end": 112.65,
          "en": "for every tick of our animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 115.32300000000001,
          "en": "So for example, 60 times per second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.37,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "And then inside of this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "you can update a widget's padding or margin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.113,
          "en": "or whichever value you wanna animate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.19,
          "end": 130.19,
          "en": "So for example here, I'll take my grid view like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 135.63,
          "en": "and cut it and use that as a value for this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.63,
          "end": 139.023,
          "en": "So as a return value returned by this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now in this function you also get some arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "You get a context and a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "Now the context is something we know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 150.78,
          "en": "The widget we get here is an extra widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 154.26,
          "en": "which we could add here on Animation Builder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "We could add an extra child parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "to set any widgets that maybe should be output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 162.32999999999998,
          "en": "as part of the animated content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.32999999999998,
          "end": 165.54,
          "en": "but that should not be animated themselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.54,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "And this would allow you to improve the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "of an animation by making sure that not all the items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "that are part of the animated item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 176.97,
          "en": "are rebuilt and reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.97,
          "end": 179.133,
          "en": "as long as the animation is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.709,
          "en": "And indeed, this is a feature which we can use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.709,
          "end": 187.709,
          "en": "to actually set our grid view here as a child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "by cutting it again and setting it as a child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "And by then adding a, let's say, padding widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.485,
          "en": "which is then the actual widget that will be animated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.485,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "which child is set to this child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 204.363,
          "en": "which is the grid view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 208.56,
          "en": "And therefore the grid view would technically be displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.56,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "inside of the padding, but it would not be rebuilt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 215.04,
          "en": "and reevaluated 60 times per second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.04,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "Only the padding widget would be rebuilt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "and reevaluated that often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "And from a performance perspective,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 225.48,
          "en": "that's of course preferable to re-executing everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.48,
          "end": 226.313,
          "en": "that often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 230.31,
          "en": "Now the padding widget also needs a padding value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.31,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "And here I now wanna set a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 235.653,
          "en": "that's dynamically animated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.61,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "And for this we can of course again use edge insets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 243.24,
          "en": "but now here I'll use edge insets only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.24,
          "end": 245.52,
          "en": "to set the padding to the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.52,
          "end": 249.063,
          "en": "And this padding value should now be set dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.05,
          "end": 254.07,
          "en": "It should be set dynamically based on these bound values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.07,
          "end": 256.08299999999997,
          "en": "between which I'm animating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 259.62,
          "en": "And the animation controller will start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.62,
          "end": 264.09,
          "en": "at a value of zero and end after 300 milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.09,
          "end": 265.263,
          "en": "at a value of one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 269.7,
          "en": "They offer to animate my padding here, my top padding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.7,
          "end": 274,
          "en": "I could set this equal to animationController.value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 279.15,
          "en": "which gives me access to the current value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 282.54,
          "en": "which will be between zero and one as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.54,
          "end": 286.02,
          "en": "times 100 for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.02,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "Now we would animate up to a padding of 100",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 292.65,
          "en": "because initially animation controller value is zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.65,
          "end": 295.68,
          "en": "and zero times 100 is zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.68,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "But at the end, after 300 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 300.39,
          "en": "we would have a value of one here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.39,
          "end": 302.34,
          "en": "and therefore the padding would be one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 303.45,
          "end": 305.43,
          "en": "Now if I do that and save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.43,
          "end": 309.09,
          "en": "we can therefore see if I go to favorites and back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.09,
          "end": 311.73,
          "en": "nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 311.73,
          "end": 314.97,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that indeed out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.97,
          "end": 317.97,
          "en": "just by adding such an animation controller,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.97,
          "end": 320.373,
          "en": "the animation will not be played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 324.36,
          "en": "To play it, you have to explicitly start it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 324.36,
          "end": 326.37,
          "en": "And we can do this here in initState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 328.92,
          "en": "right after creating it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.92,
          "end": 332.19,
          "en": "For this, you can target the animation controller again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 332.19,
          "end": 334.77,
          "en": "and then here you got various controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.77,
          "end": 337.56,
          "en": "For example, you can stop it with stop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 337.56,
          "end": 340.2,
          "en": "if you would want to pause it whilst it's playing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.2,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "for example, because a user tapped some widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 345.54,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 345.54,
          "end": 348.753,
          "en": "And you can also start it by calling forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 353.73,
          "en": "This will start the animation and play it to its end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.73,
          "end": 355.743,
          "en": "unless you stop it in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 359.34000000000003,
          "en": "You can also use repeat instead of forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.34000000000003,
          "end": 361.44,
          "en": "so that it would repeat the animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.44,
          "end": 364.08,
          "en": "and always restart it once it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 364.08,
          "end": 366.54,
          "en": "But here I'll go for forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 366.54,
          "end": 370.29,
          "en": "And with that, if you save this and then restart this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 370.29,
          "end": 373.95,
          "en": "you will see that indeed if I go to favorites and back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 373.95,
          "end": 378.003,
          "en": "this animation plays, and it slides down these items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 378.87,
          "end": 381.87,
          "en": "but wait a second slides down?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 381.87,
          "end": 383.943,
          "en": "I wanted to slide them up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384.96,
          "end": 387.6,
          "en": "Well, we simply have to adjust our logic down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 387.6,
          "end": 389.58,
          "en": "in the Animated Builder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 389.58,
          "end": 392.55,
          "en": "Currently I'm animating from zero to 100 here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 392.55,
          "end": 394.17,
          "en": "with this logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 394.17,
          "end": 397.89,
          "en": "To slide my items down, we should change this logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 397.89,
          "end": 401.46,
          "en": "and for example, set the padding to the top to 100",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 401.46,
          "end": 406.053,
          "en": "minus animation controller value times 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 407.25,
          "end": 409.35,
          "en": "This will initially be zero and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 409.35,
          "end": 412.71,
          "en": "therefore will start at a padding to the top of 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 412.71,
          "end": 414.33,
          "en": "And by the end of the animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 414.33,
          "end": 417.03,
          "en": "animation controller value will be one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 417.03,
          "end": 421.53,
          "en": "So this here will be 100 and 100 minus 100 will be zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 421.53,
          "end": 423.36,
          "en": "So therefore, at the end of the animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 423.36,
          "end": 425.88,
          "en": "the padding to the top will be zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 425.88,
          "end": 428.13,
          "en": "And with that it should indeed slide up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 428.13,
          "end": 431.31,
          "en": "So if we save this ,now this looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 431.31,
          "end": 435.123,
          "en": "And now I got this animation as I switch to this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 436.08,
          "end": 439.036,
          "en": "But by the way, not if I come from the filters screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 439.036,
          "end": 443.49,
          "en": "because here this categories screen was never removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 443.49,
          "end": 445.14,
          "en": "from the stack of screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 445.14,
          "end": 447.36,
          "en": "That's different with favorites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 447.36,
          "end": 450.3,
          "en": "And the animation, of course, only restarts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 450.3,
          "end": 452.97,
          "en": "if the widget is re-added to the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 452.97,
          "end": 455.31,
          "en": "because we started in initState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 455.31,
          "end": 459.75,
          "en": "and initState is only executed when the widget is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 459.75,
          "end": 461.97,
          "en": "When we move to the filters screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 461.97,
          "end": 464.7,
          "en": "the categories screen is still on the stack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 464.7,
          "end": 467.19,
          "en": "and it's not recreated if we come back to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 467.19,
          "end": 468.96,
          "en": "It's just shown again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 468.96,
          "end": 471.27,
          "en": "That's why we don't get the animation here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 471.27,
          "end": 473.73,
          "en": "but why we do get it if we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 473.73,
          "end": 476.34000000000003,
          "en": "come back from the favorites screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 476.34000000000003,
          "end": 479.61,
          "en": "So that's how you can add explicit animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 479.61,
          "end": 483.12,
          "en": "by adding such a animation controller, configuring it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 483.12,
          "end": 484.789,
          "en": "starting the animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 484.789,
          "end": 489.09,
          "en": "and then also controlling what should be animated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 489.09,
          "end": 491.19,
          "en": "for example, the padding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 491.19,
          "end": 492.42,
          "en": "And here as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 492.42,
          "end": 495.69,
          "en": "we're also using the performance optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 495.69,
          "end": 497.61,
          "en": "of putting the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 497.61,
          "end": 501.12,
          "en": "that actually should only be part of the animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 501.12,
          "end": 503.22,
          "en": "but which should not be rebuilt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 503.22,
          "end": 505.92,
          "en": "because its values don't change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 505.92,
          "end": 509.1,
          "en": "by putting that content into the separate child here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 509.1,
          "end": 512.37,
          "en": "so that it's included in the animated content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 512.37,
          "end": 513.87,
          "en": "but not rebuilt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 513.87,
          "end": 517.293,
          "en": "which helps us with improving the application's performance.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
